Helper `withPostcode` (line 129) puts `"2000"`; `structuredOwner` (line 136) also uses postcode `"2000"`. There is no dedicated unit test for `CityRegion`/`RegionPostcodes`/`ValidatePostcode` — only these acceptance tests.

### 5. Package structure

Root Maven project (`org.springframework.samples.petclinic`), source under `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/`:
- `util/` — `CityRegion.java`, `RegionPostcodes.java` (the two pinned lookup tables), plus peers `ContactPreference`, `MembershipLevel`, `BusinessDay`.
- `rest/function/owner/` — OfficeFloor pipeline steps: `ValidatePostcode.java`, `RespondWithOwner.java`, `ApplyOwner.java`, `NormalizeAddress.java`, `AddressNormalizer.java`, `BuildOwner.java`, etc.
- `rest/escalation/` — `InvalidPostcodeException.java` + `InvalidPostcodeExceptionHandler.java` (mirrored by a YAML file under `src/main/resources/officefloor/escalation/`).
- `mapper/OwnerMapper.java` — MapStruct interface computing the `locality` response field.
- `model/Owner.java` — persists `city` and `postcode`.
- `src/main/resources/openapi.yml` — API schema documenting `postcode` (input) and `locality` (read-only output).
